														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3880328">
									

<p>Novote. I don't feel like I get anything out of this, but I also don't have any general disliking for this type of grimdark-goofy short narrative.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;D-3356's body is non-anomalous. Hume readings have proven so.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That bothers me, though. Humes are a measurement of <em>specifically reality-distorting</em> anomalous effects, not just something being anomalous in some way in general. (I mean, people can interpret the canon however they want, but that interpretation was always super unbelievable to me &#8212; it's like detecting someone's temperature, height, weight, and blood type with a voltmeter. 'Anomalous' can mean many things, not just physics-affecting. It just plain doesn't make sense.)</p>

							</div>

								
					
